//RS // ── D-SERVICE1=D (#444): sema-known structured service tree over supervisor groups ─
//RS // Beginner topology: named tree → workers with typed mailboxes → OneForOne
//RS // restart policy. Delivery is at-most-once with Full under capacity (D-SERVICE-
//RS // DELIVERY1). Engines marshal into these Prelude symbols only (I9).
//RS //
//RS // Supervision reuses the ratified concurrency substrate rather than restating
//RS // it: a supervisor is a task that owns a `JetTaskGroupRuntime` child group
//RS // (D-CONC-GROUP1/D-CONC-SCHED1), a restart rule is data on that group, and a
//RS // failure is the one `JetTaskFailure` rail from Prelude/TaskGroup.rs.
//RS // Workflow activity attempts have their own recorded service result row:
//RS // `TaskOutcome` is the attempt/run result and `TaskStatus` is the wait state.
//RS // They are typed values at the API and replay boundary, never status strings.
//RS 
